1
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,640
[HOST] Welcome back to Amber Eyes.

2
00:00:25,290 --> 00:00:29,622
Today, we officially inaugurate Season
Two under the overarching theme:

3
00:00:29,622 --> 00:00:32,490
Psychological Manipulation
and Hands-Off Crime.

4
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:35,381
Imagine a homicide
without a murder weapon,

5
00:00:35,381 --> 00:00:37,920
devoid of physical fingerprints
at the crime scene.

6
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:42,190
The two central figures were separated
by over fifty kilometers of road.

7
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:46,660
Yet a seventeen-year-old high school girl
was convicted of involuntary manslaughter.

8
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:50,790
All of it originated solely
from digital text messages.

9
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,827
[HOST] The morning of July 13th, 2014,

10
00:00:53,827 --> 00:00:58,940
in the parking lot of a Kmart store in the
coastal town of Fairhaven, Massachusetts.

11
00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:01,675
Amidst the oppressive summer heat,

12
00:01:01,675 --> 00:01:04,066
a black Ford F-250 pickup truck had sat

13
00:01:04,066 --> 00:01:07,070
motionless for hours in
the most secluded corner.

14
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:11,780
When a store security guard walked over to
investigate, it was already far too late.

15
00:01:12,730 --> 00:01:14,559
[HOST] Inside the cabin lay the body of

16
00:01:14,559 --> 00:01:17,130
eighteen-year-old Conrad
Henri Roy the Third.

17
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:21,718
He had breathed his last in
an environment saturated with

18
00:01:21,718 --> 00:01:25,240
lethal toxic fumes generated by
a gasoline-powered water pump.

19
00:01:26,290 --> 00:01:27,387
Surveying the scene,

20
00:01:27,387 --> 00:01:30,021
everyone initially assumed
this was an agonizing

21
00:01:30,021 --> 00:01:32,490
yet strictly private
act of self-destruction.

22
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:35,120
Conrad Roy was not a delinquent youth.

23
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:39,827
He was a handsome young man who had just
graduated from high school with honors

24
00:01:39,827 --> 00:01:44,350
and earned his tugboat captain’s license
to carry on his family’s maritime legacy.

25
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,380
Yet behind that gentle
smile was a fragile soul.

26
00:01:48,730 --> 00:01:52,730
He constantly wrestled with severe
clinical depression and persistent anxiety.

27
00:01:54,030 --> 00:01:56,597
[LYNN ROY] That entire morning,
I called Conrad repeatedly,

28
00:01:56,597 --> 00:01:58,790
but his phone went straight to voicemail.

29
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:03,260
A mother’s intuition whispered to
me that the worst had come to pass.

30
00:02:03,810 --> 00:02:07,170
When police informed me they
found his truck in the Kmart lot,

31
00:02:07,170 --> 00:02:08,850
my heart shattered into pieces.

32
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:14,540
I blamed myself in agonizing grief for
failing to rescue my son from his depression.

33
00:02:15,090 --> 00:02:18,890
At the time, I assumed my boy had
simply grown too weary of this life.

34
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:23,054
I had no inkling that an
invisible hand had pushed

35
00:02:23,054 --> 00:02:25,660
my child to his death
from dozens of miles away.

36
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:30,900
[HOST] The case seemed destined to be
closed as a sorrowful domestic tragedy.

37
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:32,006
However,

38
00:02:32,006 --> 00:02:35,081
standard forensic protocol
required law enforcement to

39
00:02:35,081 --> 00:02:38,270
secure and catalog all personal
effects of the deceased.

40
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:41,060
Among those effects was
Conrad’s smartphone.

41
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:45,780
[INVESTIGATOR] I am Detective Scott
Gordon of the Fairhaven Police Department.

42
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:50,941
When we connected Conrad’s phone to
digital forensic extraction software,

43
00:02:50,941 --> 00:02:53,784
a vast repository of
over twenty thousand text

44
00:02:53,784 --> 00:02:56,750
messages and hundreds of
call logs materialized.

45
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:01,355
The individual communicating most
frequently with the victim in his final

46
00:03:01,355 --> 00:03:05,260
days was a seventeen-year-old female
student named Michelle Carter.

47
00:03:05,610 --> 00:03:08,475
And what we uncovered within
that digital transcript

48
00:03:08,475 --> 00:03:11,010
sent shockwaves through
our entire department.

49
00:03:12,510 --> 00:03:14,241
[HOST] These were not words of comfort or

50
00:03:14,241 --> 00:03:16,430
heartfelt counsel from
a caring girlfriend.

51
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:19,375
It was a systematic campaign of coercion,

52
00:03:19,375 --> 00:03:22,051
a ruthless psychological
trap engineered to ensure

53
00:03:22,051 --> 00:03:24,620
the eighteen-year-old
youth could not turn back.

54
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:27,305
[PSYCHOLOGIST] In clinical psychology,

55
00:03:27,305 --> 00:03:30,490
an individual in the throes
of acute depression possesses

56
00:03:30,490 --> 00:03:33,340
an exceptionally fragile
and impressionable psyche.

57
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:37,030
They constantly oscillate
between the instinct for survival

58
00:03:37,030 --> 00:03:39,710
and the desperate longing
to end their mental agony.

59
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:43,710
If during that critical juncture
a trusted confidant persistently

60
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:46,798
reinforces that quitting life
is the only valid choice,

61
00:03:46,798 --> 00:03:48,820
their final lifeline is obliterated.

62
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:53,725
[HOST] The discovery of that mobile
phone in the Kmart parking lot launched a

63
00:03:53,725 --> 00:03:57,640
digital investigation unprecedented in
the annals of American jurisprudence.

64
00:03:58,290 --> 00:04:02,396
An arena where written words were no
longer mere vehicles of conversation,

65
00:04:02,396 --> 00:04:05,170
but had transformed into
invisible lethal weapons.

66
00:04:08,170 --> 00:04:10,466
[HOST] To comprehend the
origins of this tragedy,

67
00:04:10,466 --> 00:04:12,761
detectives had to reconstruct the peculiar

68
00:04:12,761 --> 00:04:15,330
history between Conrad
Roy and Michelle Carter.

69
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:18,976
The pair first met in 2012
in Florida while on vacation

70
00:04:18,976 --> 00:04:21,700
with their respective
families visiting relatives.

71
00:04:22,050 --> 00:04:25,770
At that time, Conrad was sixteen,
while Michelle was merely fifteen.

72
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:29,712
[INVESTIGATOR] The most striking
aspect of this relationship was the

73
00:04:29,712 --> 00:04:33,210
geographic proximity contrasted
with their mode of interaction.

74
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:36,300
Michelle Carter resided in Plainville,

75
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:40,860
roughly thirty-five miles from Conrad’s
home—less than an hour’s drive.

76
00:04:41,210 --> 00:04:43,762
Yet across more than
two years of courtship,

77
00:04:43,762 --> 00:04:47,010
they met in person on only a
handful of brief occasions.

78
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:51,288
Their relationship existed almost
entirely within cyberspace,

79
00:04:51,288 --> 00:04:56,440
sustained through thousands of text
messages, emails, and overnight phone calls.

80
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,115
[HOST] For the majority of that time,

81
00:04:59,115 --> 00:05:01,720
Michelle Carter appeared to
be a supportive listener.

82
00:05:02,370 --> 00:05:05,416
Both harbored personal emotional
struggles and frequently

83
00:05:05,416 --> 00:05:08,730
confided regarding academic
stress and feelings of loneliness.

84
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:11,524
Michelle had even
previously urged Conrad to

85
00:05:11,524 --> 00:05:14,080
consult psychologists
and medical specialists.

86
00:05:15,230 --> 00:05:17,205
However, entering early July 2014,

87
00:05:17,205 --> 00:05:19,761
a chilling and grotesque
transformation took

88
00:05:19,761 --> 00:05:22,550
place within the
seventeen-year-old girl’s mind.

89
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:26,515
Instead of encouraging her boyfriend
to seek medical intervention,

90
00:05:26,515 --> 00:05:28,980
Michelle Carter executed
a complete reversal.

91
00:05:29,330 --> 00:05:32,577
She actively formulated plans
and incessantly badgered Conrad

92
00:05:32,577 --> 00:05:35,770
to carry out his self-destructive
impulse to the bitter end.

93
00:05:37,070 --> 00:05:41,573
[INVESTIGATOR] The transcripts we
extracted between July 2nd and July 12th,

94
00:05:41,573 --> 00:05:44,350
2014, are genuinely chilling to read.

95
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:50,680
Michelle texted Conrad: "You always say
you’re gonna do it, but then you don’t.

96
00:05:52,130 --> 00:05:54,490
I bet tonight you'll make an excuse again.

97
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:58,120
The time is right and you're
ready, you just need to do it.

98
00:05:58,470 --> 00:05:59,990
No more pushing it off.

99
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:01,380
Just do it.

100
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:05,624
[HOST] When Conrad voiced
terror regarding the agony his

101
00:06:05,624 --> 00:06:08,052
parents and two younger
sisters would suffer,

102
00:06:08,052 --> 00:06:11,020
Michelle ruthlessly dismantled
his final moral barrier.

103
00:06:11,970 --> 00:06:14,930
She texted him: "Your
family will understand.

104
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:19,880
They will be sad for a while, but then
they“ll know that you”re in a better place.

105
00:06:20,230 --> 00:06:21,990
They will accept it and move on.

106
00:06:23,490 --> 00:06:26,350
[PSYCHOLOGIST] This represents an
intensely hazardous manipulative

107
00:06:26,350 --> 00:06:28,650
tactic known as Escalation of Commitment.

108
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:31,792
The manipulator does not
wield physical force,

109
00:06:31,792 --> 00:06:35,260
but targets the victim's self-esteem
and vulnerability to shame.

110
00:06:35,610 --> 00:06:37,974
By implanting into
Conrad’s mind the notion

111
00:06:37,974 --> 00:06:40,392
that failing to act was
an act of cowardice,

112
00:06:40,392 --> 00:06:43,690
Michelle backed a youth in
crisis into an impossible corner.

113
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:46,014
In Conrad’s impressionable perception,

114
00:06:46,014 --> 00:06:48,039
stepping back meant admitting he was an

115
00:06:48,039 --> 00:06:50,480
absolute failure in the
eyes of his girlfriend.

116
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:56,900
[HOST] On the night of July 12th, 2014,
that psychological snare snapped shut.

117
00:06:57,550 --> 00:07:01,150
Conrad drove his pickup truck to
the deserted Kmart parking lot.

118
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:05,534
Inside the vehicle cabin, he switched
on the gasoline-powered water pump,

119
00:07:05,534 --> 00:07:08,020
allowing noxious exhaust
fumes to accumulate.

120
00:07:09,270 --> 00:07:11,659
Yet at that threshold
between life and death,

121
00:07:11,659 --> 00:07:15,110
the powerful human instinct for
self-preservation surged forward.

122
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:17,820
Conrad panicked.

123
00:07:18,170 --> 00:07:19,434
Overcome by asphyxiation,

124
00:07:19,434 --> 00:07:22,770
he opened the truck door and stepped
out into the clean night air.

125
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:26,040
He dialed Michelle Carter on
his phone seeking a lifeline.

126
00:07:26,390 --> 00:07:30,430
Yet what he received in return was not
a hand pulling him back into the light.

127
00:07:31,730 --> 00:07:34,770
[INVESTIGATOR] Their phone connection
persisted for over forty minutes.

128
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:39,440
When Conrad expressed terror
and insisted he wanted to stop,

129
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:43,660
Michelle Carter did not dial 911,
nor did she alert his family.

130
00:07:44,010 --> 00:07:47,919
Instead, she issued an
unequivocal command over the line:

131
00:07:47,919 --> 00:07:50,250
Get back in the truck immediately.

132
00:07:54,950 --> 00:07:57,434
[HOST] The paramount question
that left the American

133
00:07:57,434 --> 00:08:00,249
public utterly stunned when
the file unraveled was:

134
00:08:00,249 --> 00:08:00,470
Why?

135
00:08:01,670 --> 00:08:05,777
What underlying drive would compel a
seventeen-year-old girl from an affluent

136
00:08:05,777 --> 00:08:09,670
suburban family to coldly push her
boyfriend toward his demise from afar?

137
00:08:10,970 --> 00:08:14,253
[PSYCHOLOGIST] The answer resides
within a complex clinical pathology:

138
00:08:14,253 --> 00:08:18,850
Histrionic Personality Disorder intertwined
with Digital Munchausen Syndrome.

139
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:23,843
Individuals suffering from this dynamic
harbor a pathological craving to remain the

140
00:08:23,843 --> 00:08:25,888
center of dramatic attention and receive

141
00:08:25,888 --> 00:08:28,240
unconditional sympathy
from those around them.

142
00:08:28,590 --> 00:08:30,846
They cannot tolerate
feelings of being ordinary

143
00:08:30,846 --> 00:08:32,670
or overlooked within their peer group.

144
00:08:33,870 --> 00:08:35,852
[HOST] At King Philip
Regional High School,

145
00:08:35,852 --> 00:08:38,110
Michelle Carter was a peripheral student.

146
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:41,242
She possessed few close
friends and constantly

147
00:08:41,242 --> 00:08:43,400
perceived herself as socially alienated.

148
00:08:43,750 --> 00:08:45,395
To pursue external validation,

149
00:08:45,395 --> 00:08:48,355
Michelle retreated into an
elaborate fantasy construct

150
00:08:48,355 --> 00:08:51,590
nurtured by popular entertainment
and social media culture.

151
00:08:52,590 --> 00:08:54,780
[INVESTIGATOR] During
electronic device examinations,

152
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:57,603
we uncovered Michelle
Carter’s profound obsession

153
00:08:57,603 --> 00:08:59,850
with the television musical drama Glee,

154
00:08:59,850 --> 00:09:02,270
particularly its lead actress Lea Michele.

155
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:07,379
In 2013, actor Cory Monteith,
Lea Michele’s real-life partner,

156
00:09:07,379 --> 00:09:10,760
passed away suddenly from
a substance overdose.

157
00:09:11,110 --> 00:09:16,002
In the aftermath, Lea Michele was
enveloped by boundless public affection,

158
00:09:16,002 --> 00:09:18,910
protective embrace, and
worldwide adoration.

159
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:21,933
Michelle Carter copied
lines verbatim from that

160
00:09:21,933 --> 00:09:25,060
television series to send to
Conrad and her classmates.

161
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:29,120
[HOST] Michelle Carter desired
a public tragedy of her own.

162
00:09:29,770 --> 00:09:32,838
She sought to inhabit the role
of the grieving girlfriend,

163
00:09:32,838 --> 00:09:35,218
a saintly figure
shouldering profound loss to

164
00:09:35,218 --> 00:09:37,810
garner consoling embraces
and communal reverence.

165
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:42,880
Yet for that theatrical performance to stage
its premiere, Conrad Roy had to perish.

166
00:09:44,330 --> 00:09:46,715
Michelle’s calculating
premeditation was so

167
00:09:46,715 --> 00:09:49,155
horrifying that days
before Conrad’s demise,

168
00:09:49,155 --> 00:09:50,930
she began rehearsing her script.

169
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:55,507
She messaged schoolmates claiming
Conrad was already missing,

170
00:09:55,507 --> 00:09:57,080
feigning overwhelming dread.

171
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:59,432
Whereas in reality at that very moment,

172
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:01,948
Conrad was sitting peacefully
watching television

173
00:10:01,948 --> 00:10:03,950
beside his family in their living room.

174
00:10:05,450 --> 00:10:08,136
[PSYCHOLOGIST] Fabricating an
online crisis prior to the event

175
00:10:08,136 --> 00:10:11,050
demonstrates this was no
sudden adolescent impulse.

176
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:14,735
Michelle had drafted the
sorrowful narrative for her life,

177
00:10:14,735 --> 00:10:16,462
designated each character’s role,

178
00:10:16,462 --> 00:10:20,020
and the only missing element was
the actual demise of her boyfriend.

179
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:21,596
When Conrad hesitated,

180
00:10:21,596 --> 00:10:24,495
his act of exiting the truck
threatened to dismantle

181
00:10:24,495 --> 00:10:27,450
the grand scenario she had
painstakingly constructed.

182
00:10:28,750 --> 00:10:30,065
[HOST] The moment Conrad was dead,

183
00:10:30,065 --> 00:10:33,670
Michelle Carter stepped onto the public
stage she had desperately coveted.

184
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:37,320
She posted tearful tributes
across Facebook and Twitter.

185
00:10:37,670 --> 00:10:41,056
She spearheaded a regional charity
baseball tournament named Homers

186
00:10:41,056 --> 00:10:44,190
for Conrad to raise funds and
promote mental health awareness.

187
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:47,940
Crucially, the tournament was not
hosted in the victim’s hometown.

188
00:10:48,290 --> 00:10:50,648
It was staged right in
Michelle’s home community,

189
00:10:50,648 --> 00:10:54,690
where she positioned herself at the center
of local news coverage and public praise.

190
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:57,981
The angelic girlfriend mask
appeared to have secured

191
00:10:57,981 --> 00:11:00,140
Michelle Carter the
defining role of her life.

192
00:11:01,690 --> 00:11:05,970
Until her own arrogance and compulsive
need to boast stripped that facade away.

193
00:11:08,970 --> 00:11:11,451
[HOST] The true cause behind
Conrad Roy’s death might

194
00:11:11,451 --> 00:11:13,770
have remained forever
shrouded in darkness.

195
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:15,201
Yet it did not,

196
00:11:15,201 --> 00:11:17,594
because Michelle Carter
could not suppress her

197
00:11:17,594 --> 00:11:20,300
pathological urge to overshare
across phone screens.

198
00:11:21,150 --> 00:11:24,753
On September 15th, 2014, two
months following Conrad’s death,

199
00:11:24,753 --> 00:11:27,412
Michelle dispatched a
fateful confession text

200
00:11:27,412 --> 00:11:30,070
to her close school
friend Samantha Boardman.

201
00:11:31,270 --> 00:11:34,702
[SAMANTHA] That day, when I opened
my phone and read Michelle’s text,

202
00:11:34,702 --> 00:11:36,950
my hands began shaking uncontrollably.

203
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:41,620
Michelle wrote to me verbatim:
"Conrad's death is my fault.

204
00:11:43,070 --> 00:11:45,590
Like, honestly, I could have stopped him.

205
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:48,867
I was on the phone with
him and he got out of the

206
00:11:48,867 --> 00:11:50,820
car because he was scared
and it was working.

207
00:11:51,370 --> 00:11:52,650
And I told him to get back in.

208
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:55,160
I could not believe what I was reading.

209
00:11:55,710 --> 00:11:58,869
The girl who had been crying
every day playing the devastated

210
00:11:58,869 --> 00:12:02,390
girlfriend was the one who ordered
Conrad back into that toxic trap.

211
00:12:02,940 --> 00:12:05,980
I knew right then I could not
stay silent another second.

212
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:10,464
[HOST] That written confession
provided the incontrovertible

213
00:12:10,464 --> 00:12:12,491
evidence enabling the Bristol County

214
00:12:12,491 --> 00:12:15,025
District Attorney’s
Office to indict Michelle

215
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:17,840
Carter for involuntary
manslaughter in early 2015.

216
00:12:18,590 --> 00:12:22,150
An unprecedented legal confrontation
officially got underway.

217
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:27,580
In June 2017, inside the Bristol County
Juvenile Court in Taunton, Massachusetts.

218
00:12:27,930 --> 00:12:30,743
Michelle Carter entered the
courtroom flanked by dozens

219
00:12:30,743 --> 00:12:33,250
of national and international
television cameras.

220
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:37,560
To avoid emotional public judgment,
Carter made a calculated gamble.

221
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:40,748
She waived her constitutional
right to a jury trial,

222
00:12:40,748 --> 00:12:44,950
placing her entire fate in the hands of
a single judge: Judge Lawrence Moniz.

223
00:12:46,250 --> 00:12:48,489
[INVESTIGATOR] Defense
counsel Joseph Cataldo argued

224
00:12:48,489 --> 00:12:50,849
vigorously that Michelle Carter was not

225
00:12:50,849 --> 00:12:55,570
physically present at the scene and
exerted no physical force upon the victim.

226
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:59,531
He invoked First Amendment
freedom of speech protections,

227
00:12:59,531 --> 00:13:02,900
claiming mere words could not
legally constitute homicide.

228
00:13:03,250 --> 00:13:04,039
In contrast,

229
00:13:04,039 --> 00:13:07,525
Chief Prosecutor Katie
Rayburn projected thousands of

230
00:13:07,525 --> 00:13:11,010
incriminating text messages
across courtroom screens.

231
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:14,301
She demonstrated that Carter’s
pressure was continuous,

232
00:13:14,301 --> 00:13:16,440
deliberate, and methodically calculated.

233
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,453
[PSYCHOLOGIST] The defense
even retained a prominent

234
